Slipstream is designed for serious writing and deep reading. In standard mode, notes are constrained to an optimal reading width of `72ch` (max `840px`), preventing long lines that fatigue the eyes during extended research or drafting.

> [!TIP]
> **Check the Outline Tab**: Look over at the **Right Context Inspector** (or click `◨` in the top bar if it's closed). The **Outline** tab automatically analyzes this document's headings and renders a clickable, hierarchical table of contents!

---

! Level 1 Heading: The Foundation

Typography in Slipstream uses modern, fluid typography tokens and native TiddlyWiki palette variables (`--tpc-*` and `--tp-*`). This ensures that regardless of whether you choose a light theme, dark theme, or custom palette, contrast ratios and readability remain pristine.

!! Level 2 Heading: Formatting Elements

You can format your writing with standard wikitext and markdown:

* ''Bold text'' and //italic text// for emphasis
* ~~Strikethrough~~ and `inline code fragments`
* Mathematical symbols and technical terms: $E = mc^2$ or `Array.prototype.map()`
* External links and internal wiki links: [[Welcome to Slipstream]] and [[Knowledge Base]]

!!! Level 3 Heading: Quotes & Callouts

> "Simplicity is prerequisite for reliability."
> — Edsger W. Dijkstra

Blockquotes are styled with a clean accent border and subtle background tint that harmonizes with your active palette.

!! Tables & Structured Data

Tables in Slipstream adapt cleanly to the content area with clear column alignments and bordered cells:

| !Feature | !Standard View | !Wide View |
| Reading Width | `840px` (72ch optimal) | `1120px` (Expanded) |
| Best For | Prose, Essays, Research Notes | Dashboards, Databases, Large Tables |
| Trigger | Default behavior | Tagged `Wide` or `page-width: wide` |
| Inspector Integration | Fully responsive | Supported |

!! Code Blocks

Slipstream renders fenced code blocks with clean padding and monospaced typography:

```javascript
// Filter helper example
function getActiveNotes(wiki, tag) {
  return wiki.filterTiddlers(`[tag[${tag}]!has[draft.of]sort[title]]`);
}
```

